Q: Multiply two columns within a CodeIgniter select_sum() call A: <p>Using parentheses in the first parameter of <code>select_sum()</code> will disable the identifier quoting and render a valid query.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function getStockValue(): ?float
{
    return $this-&gt;db
        -&gt;select_sum('(product_price * product_quantity)', 'stockvalue')
        -&gt;get('products')
        -&gt;row('stockvalue');
}
</code></pre>

Q: In browser new Intl.NumberFormat(&#39;he-u-nu-hebr&#39;).format(5); prints number in latin, not Hebrew A: <p>To detect whether the numbering system is supported, you can check the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/NumberFormat/resolvedOptions#numberingsystem" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>resolvedOptions().numberingSystem</code></a> of your formatter:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const hebrFormatter = new Intl.NumberFormat('en', { numberingSystem: 'hebr' });
console.log('expected hebr', 'got',  hebrFormatter.resolvedOptions().numberingSystem);
// 'latn' if unsupported, 'hebr' otherwise.
const arabFormatter = new Intl.NumberFormat('en', { numberingSystem: 'arab' });
console.log('expected arab', 'got',  arabFormatter.resolvedOptions().numberingSystem);</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>Note that <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/NumberFormat/supportedLocalesOf" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>supportedLocalesOf()</code></a> (both with <code>&quot;best-fit&quot;</code> and <code>&quot;lookup&quot;</code>)  does ignore the Unicode locale extension sequences, and thus will return true for locales that are supported even if the calendar or number system aren't.</p>

Q: How to SUM() two multiplied column values with CodeIgniter&#39;s query builder A: <p>I would suggest doing this using <code>mysql</code></p>

<pre><code>SELECT SUM(quantity * no_of_packs) as total FROM table_name WHERE sales_id = 31
</code></pre>

<p>Here is CI flavor,</p>

<pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;select('SUM(quantity * no_of_packs) as total', false);
$this-&gt;db-&gt;from('table_name');
$this-&gt;db-&gt;where('sales_id', 31);
</code></pre>

<p>Note that second argument in select will prevent CI from adding unnecessary backticks.</p>
